{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/96963-new-wave-scion","id":96963,"title":"New Wave: Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-23T11:21:37-07:00","id":96963,"title":"New Wave: Scion","content":"I'm not going to lie, this is kind of stupid, but hopefully it will be a little fun for the forum. For those who've seen the RADICAL AWESOME film the Breakfast Club I'm going ask you this, &quot;If the main teenage characters were a band of Scions, who do you think would be the best fit for their divine parent?&quot; I've already asked this stupid little question on GBN and it actually was answered ,miraculously, so maybe it get the same kind of traction here as well. <br /> <br /> Here's my answers: Andrew/Thor (The guy does have a thing against wise-cracking tricksters like John)<br /> <br /> Brian/Hephaestus (The guys a nerd (or geek, whatever the terminology) but he's not a well-respected one, and he even tries to get some revenge because of that. Sounds a lot like Hephaestus when he goes after Hera, Ares and Aphrodite for well-deserved revenge.<br /> <br /> John/Loki (Like Loki, John is one of the few tricksters who actually gets severely punished by some kind of authority figure, like Odin, or in his case principal Vernon.<br /> <br /> Molly/Amaterasu or Hera (She is a princess after all so having a parent associated with royalty makes sense in my mind) <br /> <br /> Allison/Hermes or Dionysus (Yeah, Allison looks like a goth, but for most part she's a weirdo, basket-case. Plus, she's apparently a kleptomania and compulsive liar, so that's a point for the Hermes camp.<br /> <br /> Hey, if anyone else what's to post about their favourite 80's high school movie group of outcasts and brainstorm about who their divine parent would be then go right ahead!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"react